{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate","id":1411196,"title":"New Acanthus with Questions about Fate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-31T05:37:21-07:00","id":1411196,"title":"New Acanthus with Questions about Fate","content":"Recently, myself and 3 friends picked up Chronicles of Darkness to play with out existing TTRPG group. We are rotating the ST and playing a 'Monster of the week' style campaign for now and loving it. I am playing a Acanthus and cant quite wrap my head around the intersection of Fate/Time and their practices. I've spent a few days browsing the forums trying my best to see if these questions were already answered, my apologies if I missed something.<br /> <br /> 1) Where does fate begin and end? Where does Causality fold into this? Could you use Fate: Unravelling to remove someones ability to make meaningful change to the fallen world around them? Or is that what the dice penalties represent? Could one use Patterning, to transfer an objects 'destiny' to another (Bullet wound to a friend, a wall takes damage instead of a teddy bear, etc).<br /> <br /> 2) Chaos Mastery mentions you can damage others with Hazards, would this just be likely dangers in the area? (Like a Power line blowing above them or being hit by a car). I could find the rules for Hazards, but don't know how I'd apply them reasonably.<br /> <br /> 3) We've realised that in a very mixed party (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, Mage), its quite easy for an acanthus to apply leg wrack twice at sensory range (Exceptional luck with Rote) on another supernatural creature. I worry that if its as easy as I think it is, I'll be stepping on my werewolf friends toes in 'apprehending' foes.<br /> <br /> 4) Everything has been going swimmingly so far, but is there anything I should worry about with such a mix n' match party? <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for your patience if these questions have been asked before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26395-keeperofthesporks","name":"KeeperoftheSporks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T06:43:12-07:00","id":1411208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KeeperoftheSporks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate#post1411196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Where does fate begin and end? Where does Causality fold into this? Could you use Fate: Unravelling to remove someones ability to make meaningful change to the fallen world around them? Or is that what the dice penalties represent?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You don't make people do things, but you can sure make it real hard for them not to&quot; is one of the distinguishing features of Fate \u2014 the Acanthus toolkit is very soft power-oriented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could one use Patterning, to transfer an objects 'destiny' to another (Bullet wound to a friend, a wall takes damage instead of a teddy bear, etc). </div> </div> </div>This is an established Weaving spell (see Shared Fate). It works on effects as it happens; Fate doesn't really allow you to retroactively un-harm targets on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Chaos Mastery mentions you can damage others with Hazards, would this just be likely dangers in the area? (Like a Power line blowing above them or being hit by a car). I could find the rules for Hazards, but don't know how I'd apply them reasonably. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Within the bounds of improbability&quot; suggests that yes, it's limited to stuff that it's actually possible to affect within the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) We've realised that in a very mixed party (Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling, Mage), its quite easy for an acanthus to apply leg wrack twice at sensory range (Exceptional luck with Rote) on another supernatural creature. I worry that if its as easy as I think it is, I'll be stepping on my werewolf friends toes in 'apprehending' foes. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have other things they can do without specializing, you can't be everywhere at once, and Exceptional Luck doesn't work that way on spells, as discussed most recently <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410216-the-ultimate-mastermind-fate-mind-combo?p=1410222#post1410222\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Everything has been going swimmingly so far, but is there anything I should worry about with such a mix n' match party? </div> </div> </div>Have an idea of what everyone's plans for their character are and try not to step on each other's toes in that regard \u2014 for example, if your werewolf is inclined to run down targets, maybe don't jump to Fate-induced Leg Wrack as your means of assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T07:45:13-07:00","id":1411220,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick response!<br /> <br /> It felt like a more roundabout Arcanum than Forces/Matter. It's definitely the appeal though. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411208#post1411208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an established Weaving spell (see Shared Fate). It works on effects as it happens; Fate doesn't really allow you to retroactively un-harm targets on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense. I'd wager a combination of Fate and time could pull some &quot;but you missed in the past&quot; shenanigans. But I feel like that's a whole other kettle of fish to do with Temporal Sympathy; Though that sounds like a headache to try to play out as a StoryTeller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411208#post1411208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves have other things they can do without specializing, you can't be everywhere at once, and Exceptional Luck doesn't work that way on spells, as discussed most recently <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410216-the-ultimate-mastermind-fate-mind-combo?p=1410222#post1410222\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning that Exceptional luck would easily hex a target if used as a rote. I realise I wasn't too clear on the intention!<br /> Though I thought one could give boons in the form of conditions? Though I do feel Steadfast would suck the fun out of a game very quickly (Personally, everyone enjoys different styles!). I was hoping to use it to get charmed, before going about my day. But I may definitely be confused, It's why i'm asking here after all!<br /> <br /> Thanks again for your time, you've been a massive help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26395-keeperofthesporks","name":"KeeperoftheSporks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T08:02:43-07:00","id":1411222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KeeperoftheSporks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411220#post1411220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes a lot of sense. I'd wager a combination of Fate and time could pull some &quot;but you missed in the past&quot; shenanigans. But I feel like that's a whole other kettle of fish to do with Temporal Sympathy; Though that sounds like a headache to try to play out as a StoryTeller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Temporal Summoning and Rewrite History can manage it short-term, but yeah, separate Arcanum to develop.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was meaning that Exceptional luck would easily hex a target if used as a rote. I realise I wasn't too clear on the intention! </div> </div> </div>Ah. Yeah, the main thing there is that you'll need to bump the Potency a bit to get double Leg Wrack on a Withstood spell and dump at least three Reach into instant-cast, sensory range, and Advanced Duration, and the subject can explicitly remove the Tilts before the spell ends (assuming whatever's got their legs is removable). Speed and line of sight are also a factor that complicates this, as is Paradox, potentially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T08:21:43-07:00","id":1411223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411222#post1411222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.. the subject can explicitly remove the Tilts before the spell ends (assuming whatever's got their legs is removable).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Leg Wrack lead to their legs just stop working like a curse? Or is there a mundane happenstance EG. rotten floorboards, they fall through and hurt their legs. I read it as a supernatural Hex personally. Though, On one hand a mundane explanation helps with sleepers, but leaves it open to having the offending issue solved via mundane means. <br /> <br /> Though my current character is much more reserved, I feel like fate could lead to a very &quot;action hero&quot; themed character where everything lines up perfectly for them. It would be a interesting twist on why for most blockbusters the hero lives through some crazy situation.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26395-keeperofthesporks","name":"KeeperoftheSporks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T13:38:22-07:00","id":1411241,"title":"","content":"Its something inconvenient that happens. A car passes by and the sun reflects off it and into the target's eye, accounting for the one turn duration. Their leg gets a sudden cramp or something hits it enough to cause pain without damage. The fish they ate was contaminated and now they feel sick, etc.<br /> <br /> Its what makes watching an Acanthus work so bizarre. They know what will happen, they know they made it happen, but have no clue how it will happen. They simply issue a command to the software of the universe without knowing what it will do internally to get the output on screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-31-2020, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T17:28:09-07:00","id":1411274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KeeperoftheSporks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411223#post1411223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Leg Wrack lead to their legs just stop working like a curse? Or is there a mundane happenstance EG. rotten floorboards, they fall through and hurt their legs. I read it as a supernatural Hex personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I read &quot;their legs just stop working like a curse&quot; as beyond the scope of a Ruling spell modeling exceptional bouts of luck for a target. Fate isn't really the medium of its own influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T00:02:11-07:00","id":1411300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411241#post1411241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its something inconvenient that happens. A car passes by and the sun reflects off it and into the target's eye, accounting for the one turn duration. Their leg gets a sudden cramp or something hits it enough to cause pain without damage. The fish they ate was contaminated and now they feel sick, etc.<br /> <br /> Its what makes watching an Acanthus work so bizarre. They know what will happen, they know they made it happen, but have no clue how it will happen. They simply issue a command to the software of the universe without knowing what it will do internally to get the output on screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good way of looking at it. A power that requests a &quot;what&quot; to happen, not worrying about a &quot;how&quot;. Also I might incorporate that into the character too, you're less likely to ask why you're doing something when it lines everything up neatly!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1411196-new-acanthus-with-questions-about-fate?p=1411274#post1411274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I read &quot;their legs just stop working like a curse&quot; as beyond the scope of a Ruling spell modeling exceptional bouts of luck for a target. Fate isn't really the medium of its own influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes total sense that everything that it does just looks like increasingly unlikely situations. Though i'd assume there is a threshold where sleepers start triggering paradox as it becomes harder and harder to justify with coincidence? <br /> <br /> Though I wonder how Sworn Oaths (3 dots) works. Assuming its a blind condition like the example for the sake of the question: would it be almost Promethean punishment, Birds scratching away your eyes when you violate the oath (I honestly love this idea) . Or would the fact that its now a Perfecting spell change it to be more biological chance or Magical nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26395-keeperofthesporks","name":"KeeperoftheSporks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}